#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stefan Zipproth"
msgstr "Stefan Zipproth"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Image src={stefan} alt=\"Stefan Zipproth\" width={150} />\n"
msgstr "<Image src={stefan} alt=\"Stefan Zipproth\" width={150} />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Stefan Zipproth is the lead developer and creator of Ditana. A software "
"developer from St. Ursen, Switzerland, with a background in embedded systems "
"and cross-platform development. He has worked in industries ranging from RF "
"measurement and classical image processing to AI-powered medical imaging. "
"Since 2023, he has focused on developing and refining products for the Linux "
"ecosystem. A broader overview of his work — spanning systems architecture, "
"high-performance C++, and knowledge representation — is available on his "
"[personal portfolio](https://zipproth.ch)."
msgstr ""
"Stefan Zipproth est le développeur principal et le créateur de Ditana. "
"Développeur de logiciels de St. Ursen, en Suisse, il possède une expérience "
"des systèmes embarqués et du développement multiplateforme. Il a travaillé "
"dans des secteurs allant de la mesure RF et du traitement d’images classique "
"à l’imagerie médicale assistée par l’IA. Depuis 2023, il se consacre au "
"développement et au perfectionnement de produits pour l’écosystème Linux. Un "
"aperçu plus large de ses travaux – qui couvrent l’architecture de systèmes, "
"le C++ haute performance et la représentation des connaissances – est "
"disponible sur son [portfolio personnel](https://zipproth.ch)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Through **acrion innovations GmbH**, Stefan manages the financial side of "
"Ditana while focusing solely on its development as a solo developer. This "
"structure ensures transparent stewardship of resources for the community-"
"driven project."
msgstr ""
"Par l’intermédiaire de la société **acrion innovations GmbH**, Stefan gère "
"l’aspect financier de Ditana tout en se consacrant exclusivement à son "
"développement, en tant que seul développeur. Cette structure garantit une "
"gestion transparente des ressources de ce projet porté par la communauté."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thomas Zipproth"
msgstr "Thomas Zipproth"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Image src={thomas} alt=\"Thomas Zipproth\" width={150} />\n"
msgstr "<Image src={thomas} alt=\"Thomas Zipproth\" width={150} />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Thomas Zipproth is an experienced software developer from Mindelheim, "
"Germany, with deep expertise in image processing — particularly in document "
"scanning and recognition technologies. He has spent his career working on "
"high-precision systems for automated data extraction and provides valuable "
"testing support and feedback for Ditana, helping refine its usability and "
"reliability."
msgstr ""
"Thomas Zipproth est un développeur de logiciels expérimenté de Mindelheim, "
"en Allemagne, doté d’une expertise approfondie en traitement d’images – en "
"particulier dans les technologies de numérisation et de reconnaissance de "
"documents. Il a consacré sa carrière à des systèmes de haute précision pour "
"l’extraction automatisée de données et apporte à Ditana un précieux soutien "
"en matière de tests ainsi que des retours, ce qui contribue à en affiner "
"l’ergonomie et la fiabilité."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "Acknowledgements"
msgstr "Remerciements"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Ditana would not be what it is without the contributions of others. Special "
"thanks to:"
msgstr ""
"Ditana ne serait pas ce qu’elle est sans les contributions d’autres "
"personnes. Remerciements particuliers à :"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"**Alexey Melezhik** for the [Sparrow6](https://github.com/melezhik/Sparrow6) "
"work that replaced Ansible in 0.9.3 and for ongoing collaboration on test "
"infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"**Alexey Melezhik** pour le travail sur [Sparrow6](https://github.com/"
"melezhik/Sparrow6) qui a remplacé Ansible dans la 0.9.3, et pour sa "
"collaboration continue sur l’infrastructure de test."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"**Ralf Hersel** of [gnulinux.ch](https://gnulinux.ch) for the early coverage "
"and the [podcast interview](https://gnulinux.ch/ciw119-podcast) that "
"introduced Ditana to a wider Swiss/German-speaking audience."
msgstr ""
"**Ralf Hersel**, de [gnulinux.ch](https://gnulinux.ch), pour avoir parlé de "
"Ditana dès ses débuts et pour l’[entretien en podcast](https://gnulinux.ch/"
"ciw119-podcast) qui a fait connaître Ditana à un public plus large, suisse "
"et germanophone."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Everyone who has filed an issue, sent feedback, or simply tried Ditana and "
"shared what worked or didn't."
msgstr ""
"Toutes les personnes qui ont ouvert un ticket, envoyé des retours ou "
"simplement essayé Ditana et partagé ce qui fonctionnait ou non."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"If you want to reach us: [support@ditana.org](mailto:support@ditana.org) for "
"anything at all, the [Discord channel](https://discord.gg/RgcdumdE9J) for a "
"conversation, and the issue trackers for [the installer](https://github.com/"
"acrion/ditana-installer/issues), [the configuration](https://github.com/"
"acrion/ditana-config/issues) and [the package pipeline](https://github.com/"
"acrion/ditana-build/issues) when you have something specific."
msgstr ""
"Si vous souhaitez nous joindre : [support@ditana.org]"
"(mailto:support@ditana.org) pour tout sujet, quel qu’il soit, le [canal "
"Discord](https://discord.gg/RgcdumdE9J) pour discuter, et les gestionnaires "
"de tickets [du programme d’installation](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"installer/issues), [de la configuration](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"config/issues) et [de la chaîne de production des paquets](https://"
"github.com/acrion/ditana-build/issues) lorsque vous avez une demande précise."
